  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• To a medium saucepan, add the water (for the rice) and bring to the boil.\n• Add jasmine rice and vegetable stock powder, stir, cover with a lid and reduce heat to low.\n• Cook for 12 minutes, then remove the pan from heat and keep covered until rice is tender and all the water is absorbed, 12 minutes. TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don't peak!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6523ab466c96c01e5b47010e-a033f595.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, grate carrot. Drain sweetcorn. Roughly chop baby spinach leaves. Drain and rinse black beans.\n• In a medium bowl, add sweetcorn, spinach, a drizzle of the white wine vinegar and a drizzle of olive oil. Season and set aside.\n• Roughly chop pickled jalapeños (if using). In a small bowl, combine tomato salsa and jalapeños.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6523ab466c96c01e5b47010e-e810cc0f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Add carrot and black beans and cook, stirring, until softened, 2-3 minutes.\n• SPICY! This spice blend is hot! Add less if you're sensitive to heat. Stir in tomato paste and Mexican Fiesta spice blend and cook until fragrant, 1 minute.\n• Reduce heat to medium, add the water (for the sauce) and the butter and cook, stirring, until slightly thickened, 1-2 minutes. Season.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6523ab466c96c01e5b47010e-e36df04c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide rice, fiery Mexican black beans and spinach salsa between bowls.\n• Sprinkle over Cheddar cheese.\n• Top with light sour cream and volcano sauce to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-6523ab466c96c01e5b47010e-d1a3e07e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
